@startuml
title RNF9 — Desempenho e usabilidade da interface (3D com 22 atletas) · Diagrama de sequência
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
autonumber
actor "Head coach / manager (usuário autenticado)" as Manager
participant "Frontend" as Frontend
boundary "API" as API
control "UseCase" as UseCase
database "MySQL 8" as MySQL
database "Redis 7" as Redis
database "Cassandra 4.1" as Cassandra
database "S3/MinIO" as S3
Manager -> Frontend: abre a partida ao vivo
Frontend -> API: GET /me/settings (If-None-Match)
API -> UseCase: GetUserSettingsUseCase
UseCase -> Redis: GET settings:{userId}
alt cache hit
  API --> Frontend: 304
else senão
  UseCase -> MySQL: UserSettings
  UseCase -> Redis: SET TTL 10 min
  API --> Frontend: 200 + ETag
end
alt WebGL suficiente
  Frontend -> S3: GET chunk 3D + campo + GLB atleta + texturas KTX2 (CDN, lazy)
  S3 --> Frontend: assets
  Frontend -> Frontend: 2 InstancedMesh × 11 atletas · LOD · ≤ 150 draw calls
else senão
  Frontend -> Frontend: campo 2D em SVG
end
loop partida ao vivo
  Frontend -> API: GET /matches/{mid}/events?after=seq
  API -> UseCase: GetMatchEventsUseCase
  UseCase -> Cassandra: SELECT seq > ?
  API --> Frontend: 200 / 204
  Frontend -> API: GET /matches/{mid}/formation
  API -> UseCase: GetPlayFormationUseCase
  UseCase -> Redis: posições do snap (22 × x, y)
  API --> Frontend: 200 compacto
  Frontend -> Manager: alinhamento, snap e jogada animados (ou 2D)
end
@enduml
